    "snippet": "Not only will decent moisture be in place over these areas with PWATs approaching 150-200% of normal, upper- level ascent from anti-cyclonic flow and an upper-level jet streak will provide and added layer of support for the development of shower and thunderstorm activity. Chances for SHRA/TSRA in the Phoenix airspace remain below 10% through Tuesday afternoon, with most activity remaining well to the east and southeast, however, some periods with virga showers in the vicinity cannot be ruled out",
